4f:T806,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do local service businesses build backlinks?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Start with consistent citations on Google Business Profile, Yelp, BBB and trade directories. Then earn local links from your chamber of commerce, suppliers, manufacturer installer programs, trade associations, community sponsorships and local news. A local cost guide gives other sites a reason to link to you."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are citations the same as backlinks?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not exactly. A citation is any mention of your business name, address and phone, with or without a link. Citations help Google trust your location details; backlinks help your website rank. Most directory listings give you both."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many local backlinks do I need?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Fewer than you think. In most cities, a few dozen relevant local links and consistent citations put a service business ahead of competitors who have none. Check the top three results for your \"service + city\" search to see the bar."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do sponsorship links help local SEO?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, when the sponsorship is real and local. Google treats sponsorship links as paid, so they should be marked as sponsored, but the local relevance, the visibility and the community goodwill still make them worth it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need links from national websites?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not for local rankings. A link from your cityâ€™s news site or chamber of commerce does more for \"plumber near me\" than a link from a national blog with no local audience."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this tool free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The plan, searches, progress tracking and email templates are free with no signup. The opti